  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let us define the score of an array BBB (B1,B2,B3,...,Bk)(B_1, B_2, B_3,...,B_k)(B1​,B2​,B3​,...,Bk​) as:\n\nscore(B)={∑i=1kBi,if&nbsp;k&gt;1&nbsp;and&nbsp;Max(B)−SecondMax(B)&lt;X.−∑i=1kBi,otherwise.\\begin{equation}\n  score(B)=\\begin{cases}\n    \\sum_{i=1}^{k}B_i, &amp; \\text{if } k \\gt 1 \\text{ and } Max(B) - SecondMax(B) \\lt X.\\\\\n    -\\sum_{i=1}^{k}B_i, &amp; \\text{otherwise}.\n  \\end{cases}\n\\end{equation}score(B)={∑i=1k​Bi​,−∑i=1k​Bi​,​if&nbsp;k&gt;1&nbsp;and&nbsp;Max(B)−SecondMax(B)&lt;X.otherwise.​​​Here, SecondMax(B)SecondMax(B)SecondMax(B) denotes the second element in BBB if we sort it in non-increasing order.\n\nYou are given an array AAA with NNN elements. You can partition it into multiple continuous subarrays, aiming to **maximize** the **sum of the scores** of each of the subarrays. Note that, in a partition, each element of the array belongs to **exactly** one subarray.\n\nAdditionally, you should perform QQQ queries. For each given value of XXX, find the **maximum sum of score** if you partition the array optimally.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and QQQ - the size of the array AAA and the number of queries.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains QQQ space-separated integers X1,X2,…,XQX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_QX1​,X2​,…,XQ​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output QQQ space-separated integers in a new line, the maximum sum of score you can obtain.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤3⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^52≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Xi≤1091 \\leq A_i,X_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​,Xi​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105.",
      "Sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5 3\n1 4 3 6 2\n1 4 2\n5 2\n5 7 10 1 1\n2 3",
        "output": "-16 16 0 \n-20 4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: In the third query of the first testcase, an optimal partition is [1,4,3],[6,2][1, 4, 3], [6, 2][1,4,3],[6,2]. The sum of score is (1+4+3)−(6+2)=0(1 + 4 + 3) - (6 + 2) = 0(1+4+3)−(6+2)=0.\nTest case 222: In the second query of the second testcase, an optimal partition is [5,7],[10],[1,1][5, 7], [10], [1, 1][5,7],[10],[1,1]. The sum of score is (5+7)−(10)+(1+1)=4(5 + 7) - (10) + (1 + 1) = 4(5+7)−(10)+(1+1)=4."
      }
    ]
